-- title:
--   A restart draw descriptor replays from its preceding tape interval
-- statement:
--   Let $n,r\in\mathbb N$, let $o_1,o_2$ be Boolean query functions on subsets of $[n]$, and let $s$ be an annealing schedule. A paired state is a subset of $[n]\times\{0,1\}$; a restart cursor stores such a state, a tape position, and an attempt count. Fix stored rational multiplier tables $W$ indexed by phase, a stage count $j\in\mathbb N$, an initial tape position $c\in\mathbb N$, and $k\in\{0,\ldots,3s.\mathrm{restartCap}-1\}$. The restart draw probe observes draw $k\bmod3$ of attempted chain step $\lfloor k/3\rfloor$. If this probe on tape $t$ returns descriptor $(u,D)$, then $$c\le u,\qquad \bigl[t'=t\text{ on }[c,u)\bigr]\Longrightarrow \operatorname{probe}_{t'}(k)=\operatorname{some}(u,D).$$ This holds for every tape $t$ and every returned descriptor; there is no assumption that the restart ultimately succeeds.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/RestartDrawProbeReplay.lean#L230-L266

